---
title: Code Mode
id: code-mode
order: 1
description: "Let LLMs write and execute TypeScript programs that orchestrate tools in a secure sandbox with TanStack AI Code Mode — fewer loops, richer logic."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - code mode
  - sandbox
  - typescript execution
  - tool orchestration
  - execute_typescript
  - ai agents
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode lets an LLM write and execute TypeScript programs inside a secure sandbox. Instead of making one tool call at a time, the model writes a short script that orchestrates multiple tools with loops, conditionals, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise.all"},{"type":"text","value":", and data transformations — then returns a single result."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You already have a chat app that uses "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":". By the end of this guide, you'll have Code Mode set up so the LLM can compose those tools in TypeScript and execute them in a single sandbox call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-code-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why Code Mode?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reduced-context-window-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reduced context window usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In a traditional agentic loop, every tool call adds a round-trip of messages: the model's tool-call request, the tool result, then the model's next reasoning step. A task that touches five tools can easily consume thousands of tokens in back-and-forth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With Code Mode the model emits one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" call containing a complete program. The five tool invocations happen inside the sandbox, and only the final result comes back — one request, one response."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-llm-decides-how-to-interpret-tool-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The LLM decides how to interpret tool output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When tools are called individually, the model must decide what to do with each result in a new turn. With Code Mode, the model writes the logic up front: filter, aggregate, compare, branch. It can "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise.all"},{"type":"text","value":" ten API calls, pick the best result, and return a summary — all in a single execution."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-safe-tool-execution","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-safe tool execution"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools you pass to Code Mode are converted to typed function stubs that appear in the system prompt. The model sees exact input/output types, so it generates correct calls without guessing parameter names or shapes. TypeScript annotations in the generated code are stripped automatically before execution."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"secure-sandboxing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Secure sandboxing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generated code runs in an isolated environment. V8, QuickJS WASM, native QuickJS on Bun, and a Cloudflare Worker have no access to the host file system, network, or process. A Daytona sandbox and an E2B sandbox are full Linux environments. Each sandbox has its own file system, network, and processes. The code in that sandbox cannot reach the host. Timeouts and memory limits are configurable."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"getting-started","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-install-packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install packages"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\",\"zod\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick an isolate driver:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node.js (V8 isolates, native compile):"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QuickJS WASM (browsers and edge, no native deps):"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QuickJS Bun (native QuickJS via bun:ffi):"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare Workers:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Daytona sandboxes:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona\",\"@daytona/sdk\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"E2B sandboxes:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b\",\"e2b\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-define-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Define tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define your tools with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" and provide a server-side implementation with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":". These become the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions available inside the sandbox."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst fetchWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetchWeather\",\n  description: \"Get current weather for a city\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ location: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    condition: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.weather.example/v1?city=${location}`);\n  return res.json();\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=code-mode"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-create-the-code-mode-tool-and-system-prompt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Create the Code Mode tool and system prompt"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCodeMode } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from \"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\";\n\nconst { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver: createNodeIsolateDriver(),\n  tools: [fetchWeather],\n  timeout: 30_000,\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=code-mode"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-use-with-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Use with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  systemPrompts: [\n    \"You are a helpful weather assistant.\",\n    systemPrompt,\n  ],\n  tools: [tool],\n  messages: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      content: \"Compare the weather in Tokyo, Paris, and New York City\",\n    },\n  ],\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=code-mode"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model will generate something like:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const cities = [\"Tokyo\", \"Paris\", \"New York City\"];\nconst results = await Promise.all(\n  cities.map((city) => external_fetchWeather({ location: city }))\n);\n\nconst warmest = results.reduce((prev, curr) =>\n  curr.temperature > prev.temperature ? curr : prev\n);\n\nreturn {\n  comparison: results.map((r, i) => ({\n    city: cities[i],\n    temperature: r.temperature,\n    condition: r.condition,\n  })),\n  warmest: cities[results.indexOf(warmest)],\n};","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three API calls happen in parallel inside the sandbox. The model receives one structured result instead of three separate tool-call round-trips."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createcodemode-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeMode(config)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates both the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" tool and its matching system prompt from a single config object. This is the recommended entry point."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver,          // IsolateDriver — required\n  tools,           // Array<ServerTool | ToolDefinition> — required, at least one\n  timeout,         // number — execution timeout in ms (default: 30000)\n  memoryLimit,     // number. Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers.\n  getSnippetBindings, // () => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>> — optional dynamic bindings\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Config properties:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"driver"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IsolateDriver"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The sandbox runtime to execute code in"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<ServerTool | ToolDefinition>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools exposed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" functions. Must have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".server()"},{"type":"text","value":" implementations"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timeout"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution timeout in milliseconds (default: 30000)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryLimit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Supported by Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSnippetBindings"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional function returning additional bindings at execution time"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebugOption"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug logging, same shape as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ debug })"},{"type":"text","value":". Failed executions log under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errors"},{"type":"text","value":" (on by default), successful ones under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ logger }"},{"type":"text","value":" to use your own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Logger"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to silence. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/debug-logging.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Logging"}]}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CodeModeToolResult"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface CodeModeToolResult {\n  success: boolean;\n  result?: unknown;    // Return value from the executed code\n  logs?: Array<string>; // Captured console output\n  error?: {\n    message: string;\n    name?: string;\n    line?: number;\n  };\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createcodemodetool-config-createcodemodesystemprompt-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeModeTool(config)"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lower-level functions if you need only the tool or only the prompt. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeMode"},{"type":"text","value":" calls both internally."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCodeModeTool, createCodeModeSystemPrompt } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { config } from \"./config\";\n\nconst tool = createCodeModeTool(config);\nconst prompt = createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"isolatedriver","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IsolateDriver"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The interface that sandbox runtimes implement. You do not implement this yourself — pick one of the provided drivers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { IsolateConfig, IsolateContext } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\n\ninterface IsolateDriver {\n  createContext(config: IsolateConfig): Promise<IsolateContext>;\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available drivers:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory function"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createNodeIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node.js"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuickJSIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node.js, browser, edge"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuickJSBunIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bun"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCloudflareIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare Workers"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createDaytonaIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Daytona sandboxes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createE2BIsolateDriver()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"E2B sandboxes"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For full configuration options for each driver, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-isolates.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isolate Drivers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"advanced","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These utilities are used internally and are exported for custom pipelines:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stripTypeScript(code)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Strips TypeScript syntax using sucrase (edge-safe, no native binary), converting to plain JavaScript."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsToBindings(tools, prefix?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Converts TanStack AI tools into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, ToolBinding>"},{"type":"text","value":" for sandbox injection."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTypeStubs(bindings, options?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Generates TypeScript type declarations from tool bindings for system prompts."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choosing-a-driver","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choosing a Driver"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a full comparison of drivers with all configuration options, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-isolates.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isolate Drivers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In brief: use the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node driver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for server-side Node.js (fastest, V8 JIT), "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QuickJS"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for browsers or portable edge deployments (no native deps), "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QuickJS Bun"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for Bun servers (native QuickJS via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bun:ffi"},{"type":"text","value":"), the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare driver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when you deploy to Cloudflare Workers, and the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Daytona driver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when you want execution inside a full remote Linux sandbox."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"E2B driver"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for an E2B sandbox."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode emits custom events during execution that you can observe through the TanStack AI event system. These are useful for building UIs that show execution progress, debugging, or logging."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Payload"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:execution_started"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code execution begins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ timestamp, codeLength }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:console"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.log/error/warn/info"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ level, message, timestamp }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" function runs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function, args, timestamp }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a successful "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function, result, duration }"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_mode:external_error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call fails"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ function, error, duration }"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To display these events in your React app, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./client-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing Code Mode in the UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stop-tool-calls-when-the-run-stops","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop tool calls when the run stops"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a user stops a chat run, a tool call that the sandbox started keeps going unless the tool listens for the abort. Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" call gets the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" of the chat run in its second argument. Pass it to the slow work:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst searchDocs = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchDocs\",\n  description: \"Search the docs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ query }, ctx) => {\n  const res = await fetch(\n    `https://search.example/v1?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,\n    { signal: ctx?.abortSignal },\n  );\n  return res.json();\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP tools from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-mcp"},{"type":"text","value":" already stop their request when the run aborts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool that runs inside Code Mode gets these fields:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":": the signal of the chat run. If the run is already aborted, the call does not start."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":": the runtime "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" that you gave to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":": sends a custom event to the stream. A tool that a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snippet_*"},{"type":"text","value":" function calls does not send events."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool does not get "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputResponse"},{"type":"text","value":". These fields belong to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"model-compatibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Compatibility"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode asks the model to write valid TypeScript that calls your tools through the sandbox bridge. Not every model handles this equally — many small or older models mishandle the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_*"},{"type":"text","value":" calling conventions even when the system prompt is explicit. We track a single multi-step benchmark (joining three tables, filtering customers who bought from every product category, aggregating spend per category) against a gold reference. The full harness lives at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval/"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,"center","center","center","center","center","right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rank"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stars"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Acc"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comp"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TS"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CME"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latency"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok:grok-4-1-fast-non-reasoning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★★"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7.0s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama:gpt-oss:20b"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★★"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"45.1s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"23.6k"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★★"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9.4s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8.5k"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini:gemini-2.5-flash"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★★"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7.3s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6.9k"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama:nemotron-cascade-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★★"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"60.4s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"11.7k"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openai:gpt-4o-mini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★☆"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"19.2s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8.7k"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"7"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama:gemma4:31b"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"★★☆"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"264.2s"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6.4k"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Columns"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stars"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — overall weighted rating (1-3) combining accuracy, comprehensiveness, code quality, code-mode efficiency, speed, token efficiency, and stability."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Acc / Comp / TS / CME"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Anthropic-judged subscores out of 10: accuracy vs gold, comprehensiveness, TypeScript quality, code-mode efficiency (fewer wasted attempts is better)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latency"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — wall-clock time for the full agentic loop."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tokens"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — total prompt + completion tokens. Grok's adapter does not report usage."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Takeaways"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strongest cloud picks:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Grok 4.1 Fast, Claude Haiku 4.5, and Gemini 2.5 Flash all finish under 10s and handle the multi-step task cleanly. Claude Haiku 4.5 has the highest comprehensiveness score (10/10)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strongest local pick:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama:gpt-oss:20b"},{"type":"text","value":" is the best local performer at 45s with zero compilation failures. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollama:nemotron-cascade-2"},{"type":"text","value":" is a close second."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the smaller "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemma4"},{"type":"text","value":" (9.6 GB) and the other local models commented out at the top of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"eval-config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"granite4:3b"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ministral-3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mistral:7b"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"qwen3:8b"},{"type":"text","value":", etc.) — they either ignore the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"external_queryTable"},{"type":"text","value":" shape, hallucinate results, or refuse to invoke "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute_typescript"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caveat:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" this is a single‑prompt benchmark. Local model results can vary noticeably between runs; use these as a rough capability filter rather than a definitive ranking."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reproduce locally:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"cd packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval\npnpm install\npnpm eval                    # full suite (needs cloud API keys + Anthropic for judging)\npnpm eval -- --ollama-only   # local models only\npnpm eval -- --no-judge      # skip Anthropic-based judging","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tips","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tips"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start simple."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Give the model 2-3 tools and a clear task. Code Mode works best when the model has a focused set of capabilities."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise.all"},{"type":"text","value":" tasks."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Code Mode shines when the model can parallelize work that would otherwise be sequential tool calls."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.log"},{"type":"text","value":" for debugging."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Logs are captured and returned in the result, making it easy to see what happened inside the sandbox."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep tools focused."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each tool should do one thing well. The model will compose them in code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check the system prompt."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)"},{"type":"text","value":" and inspect the output to see exactly what the model will see, including generated type stubs."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./client-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing Code Mode in the UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Display execution progress in your React app"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-with-snippets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code Mode with Snippets"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — Add persistent, reusable snippet libraries"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./code-mode-isolates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Isolate Drivers"}]},{"type":"text","value":": compare Node, QuickJS, QuickJS Bun, Cloudflare, Daytona, and E2B."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"why-code-mode","text":"Why Code Mode?","level":2},{"id":"reduced-context-window-usage","text":"Reduced context window usage","level":3},{"id":"the-llm-decides-how-to-interpret-tool-output","text":"The LLM decides how to interpret tool output","level":3},{"id":"type-safe-tool-execution","text":"Type-safe tool execution","level":3},{"id":"secure-sandboxing","text":"Secure sandboxing","level":3},{"id":"getting-started","text":"Getting Started","level":2},{"id":"1-install-packages","text":"1. Install packages","level":3},{"id":"2-define-tools","text":"2. Define tools","level":3},{"id":"3-create-the-code-mode-tool-and-system-prompt","text":"3. Create the Code Mode tool and system prompt","level":3},{"id":"4-use-with-chat","text":"4. Use with chat()","level":3},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"createcodemode-config","text":"createCodeMode(config)","level":3},{"id":"createcodemodetool-config-createcodemodesystemprompt-config","text":"createCodeModeTool(config) / createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)","level":3},{"id":"isolatedriver","text":"IsolateDriver","level":3},{"id":"advanced","text":"Advanced","level":3},{"id":"choosing-a-driver","text":"Choosing a Driver","level":2},{"id":"custom-events","text":"Custom Events","level":2},{"id":"stop-tool-calls-when-the-run-stops","text":"Stop tool calls when the run stops","level":2},{"id":"model-compatibility","text":"Model Compatibility","level":2},{"id":"tips","text":"Tips","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nCode Mode lets an LLM write and execute TypeScript programs inside a secure sandbox. Instead of making one tool call at a time, the model writes a short script that orchestrates multiple tools with loops, conditionals, `Promise.all`, and data transformations — then returns a single result.\n\nYou already have a chat app that uses [tools](../tools/tools). By the end of this guide, you'll have Code Mode set up so the LLM can compose those tools in TypeScript and execute them in a single sandbox call.\n\n## Why Code Mode?\n\n### Reduced context window usage\n\nIn a traditional agentic loop, every tool call adds a round-trip of messages: the model's tool-call request, the tool result, then the model's next reasoning step. A task that touches five tools can easily consume thousands of tokens in back-and-forth.\n\nWith Code Mode the model emits one `execute_typescript` call containing a complete program. The five tool invocations happen inside the sandbox, and only the final result comes back — one request, one response.\n\n### The LLM decides how to interpret tool output\n\nWhen tools are called individually, the model must decide what to do with each result in a new turn. With Code Mode, the model writes the logic up front: filter, aggregate, compare, branch. It can `Promise.all` ten API calls, pick the best result, and return a summary — all in a single execution.\n\n### Type-safe tool execution\n\nTools you pass to Code Mode are converted to typed function stubs that appear in the system prompt. The model sees exact input/output types, so it generates correct calls without guessing parameter names or shapes. TypeScript annotations in the generated code are stripped automatically before execution.\n\n### Secure sandboxing\n\nGenerated code runs in an isolated environment. V8, QuickJS WASM, native QuickJS on Bun, and a Cloudflare Worker have no access to the host file system, network, or process. A Daytona sandbox and an E2B sandbox are full Linux environments. Each sandbox has its own file system, network, and processes. The code in that sandbox cannot reach the host. Timeouts and memory limits are configurable.\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### 1. Install packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPick an isolate driver:\n\nNode.js (V8 isolates, native compile):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nQuickJS WASM (browsers and edge, no native deps):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nQuickJS Bun (native QuickJS via bun:ffi):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nCloudflare Workers:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nDaytona sandboxes:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nE2B sandboxes:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Define tools\n\nDefine your tools with `toolDefinition()` and provide a server-side implementation with `.server()`. These become the `external_*` functions available inside the sandbox.\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst fetchWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetchWeather\",\n  description: \"Get current weather for a city\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ location: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    condition: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.weather.example/v1?city=${location}`);\n  return res.json();\n});\n```\n\n### 3. Create the Code Mode tool and system prompt\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { createCodeMode } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from \"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\";\n\nconst { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver: createNodeIsolateDriver(),\n  tools: [fetchWeather],\n  timeout: 30_000,\n});\n```\n\n### 4. Use with `chat()`\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  systemPrompts: [\n    \"You are a helpful weather assistant.\",\n    systemPrompt,\n  ],\n  tools: [tool],\n  messages: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      content: \"Compare the weather in Tokyo, Paris, and New York City\",\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nThe model will generate something like:\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst cities = [\"Tokyo\", \"Paris\", \"New York City\"];\nconst results = await Promise.all(\n  cities.map((city) => external_fetchWeather({ location: city }))\n);\n\nconst warmest = results.reduce((prev, curr) =>\n  curr.temperature > prev.temperature ? curr : prev\n);\n\nreturn {\n  comparison: results.map((r, i) => ({\n    city: cities[i],\n    temperature: r.temperature,\n    condition: r.condition,\n  })),\n  warmest: cities[results.indexOf(warmest)],\n};\n```\n\nAll three API calls happen in parallel inside the sandbox. The model receives one structured result instead of three separate tool-call round-trips.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `createCodeMode(config)`\n\nCreates both the `execute_typescript` tool and its matching system prompt from a single config object. This is the recommended entry point.\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver,          // IsolateDriver — required\n  tools,           // Array<ServerTool | ToolDefinition> — required, at least one\n  timeout,         // number — execution timeout in ms (default: 30000)\n  memoryLimit,     // number. Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers.\n  getSnippetBindings, // () => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>> — optional dynamic bindings\n});\n```\n\n**Config properties:**\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `driver` | `IsolateDriver` | The sandbox runtime to execute code in |\n| `tools` | `Array<ServerTool \\| ToolDefinition>` | Tools exposed as `external_*` functions. Must have `.server()` implementations |\n| `timeout` | `number` | Execution timeout in milliseconds (default: 30000) |\n| `memoryLimit` | `number` | Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Supported by Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers |\n| `getSnippetBindings` | `() => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>>` | Optional function returning additional bindings at execution time |\n| `debug` | `DebugOption` | Debug logging, same shape as `chat({ debug })`. Failed executions log under `errors` (on by default), successful ones under `tools`. Pass `{ logger }` to use your own `Logger`, or `false` to silence. See [Debug Logging](../advanced/debug-logging.md) |\n\nThe tool returns a `CodeModeToolResult`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface CodeModeToolResult {\n  success: boolean;\n  result?: unknown;    // Return value from the executed code\n  logs?: Array<string>; // Captured console output\n  error?: {\n    message: string;\n    name?: string;\n    line?: number;\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### `createCodeModeTool(config)` / `createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)`\n\nLower-level functions if you need only the tool or only the prompt. `createCodeMode` calls both internally.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCodeModeTool, createCodeModeSystemPrompt } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { config } from \"./config\";\n\nconst tool = createCodeModeTool(config);\nconst prompt = createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config);\n```\n\n### `IsolateDriver`\n\nThe interface that sandbox runtimes implement. You do not implement this yourself — pick one of the provided drivers:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { IsolateConfig, IsolateContext } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\n\ninterface IsolateDriver {\n  createContext(config: IsolateConfig): Promise<IsolateContext>;\n}\n```\n\n**Available drivers:**\n\n| Package | Factory function | Environment |\n|---------|-----------------|-------------|\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-node` | `createNodeIsolateDriver()` | Node.js |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs` | `createQuickJSIsolateDriver()` | Node.js, browser, edge |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun` | `createQuickJSBunIsolateDriver()` | Bun |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare` | `createCloudflareIsolateDriver()` | Cloudflare Workers |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona` | `createDaytonaIsolateDriver()` | Daytona sandboxes |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b` | `createE2BIsolateDriver()` | E2B sandboxes |\n\nFor full configuration options for each driver, see [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates.md).\n\n### Advanced\n\nThese utilities are used internally and are exported for custom pipelines:\n\n- **`stripTypeScript(code)`** — Strips TypeScript syntax using sucrase (edge-safe, no native binary), converting to plain JavaScript.\n- **`toolsToBindings(tools, prefix?)`** — Converts TanStack AI tools into `Record<string, ToolBinding>` for sandbox injection.\n- **`generateTypeStubs(bindings, options?)`** — Generates TypeScript type declarations from tool bindings for system prompts.\n\n## Choosing a Driver\n\nFor a full comparison of drivers with all configuration options, see [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates.md).\n\nIn brief: use the **Node driver** for server-side Node.js (fastest, V8 JIT), **QuickJS** for browsers or portable edge deployments (no native deps), **QuickJS Bun** for Bun servers (native QuickJS via `bun:ffi`), the **Cloudflare driver** when you deploy to Cloudflare Workers, and the **Daytona driver** when you want execution inside a full remote Linux sandbox.\n\nUse the **E2B driver** for an E2B sandbox.\n\n## Custom Events\n\nCode Mode emits custom events during execution that you can observe through the TanStack AI event system. These are useful for building UIs that show execution progress, debugging, or logging.\n\n| Event | When | Payload |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `code_mode:execution_started` | Code execution begins | `{ timestamp, codeLength }` |\n| `code_mode:console` | Each `console.log/error/warn/info` call | `{ level, message, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:external_call` | Before an `external_*` function runs | `{ function, args, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:external_result` | After a successful `external_*` call | `{ function, result, duration }` |\n| `code_mode:external_error` | When an `external_*` call fails | `{ function, error, duration }` |\n\nTo display these events in your React app, see [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration).\n\n## Stop tool calls when the run stops\n\nWhen a user stops a chat run, a tool call that the sandbox started keeps going unless the tool listens for the abort. Each `external_*` call gets the `abortSignal` of the chat run in its second argument. Pass it to the slow work:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst searchDocs = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchDocs\",\n  description: \"Search the docs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ query }, ctx) => {\n  const res = await fetch(\n    `https://search.example/v1?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,\n    { signal: ctx?.abortSignal },\n  );\n  return res.json();\n});\n```\n\nMCP tools from `@tanstack/ai-mcp` already stop their request when the run aborts.\n\nA tool that runs inside Code Mode gets these fields:\n\n- `abortSignal`: the signal of the chat run. If the run is already aborted, the call does not start.\n- `context`: the runtime `context` that you gave to `chat()`.\n- `emitCustomEvent`: sends a custom event to the stream. A tool that a `snippet_*` function calls does not send events.\n\nThe tool does not get `toolCallId` or `inputResponse`. These fields belong to the `execute_typescript` call.\n\n## Model Compatibility\n\nCode Mode asks the model to write valid TypeScript that calls your tools through the sandbox bridge. Not every model handles this equally — many small or older models mishandle the `external_*` calling conventions even when the system prompt is explicit. We track a single multi-step benchmark (joining three tables, filtering customers who bought from every product category, aggregating spend per category) against a gold reference. The full harness lives at `packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval/`.\n\n| Rank | Model | Stars | Acc | Comp | TS | CME | Latency | Tokens |\n|------|-------|:-----:|:---:|:----:|:--:|:---:|--------:|-------:|\n| 1 | `grok:grok-4-1-fast-non-reasoning` | ★★★ | 10 | 9 | 6 | 10 | 7.0s | — |\n| 2 | `ollama:gpt-oss:20b` | ★★★ | 10 | 8 | 6 | 5 | 45.1s | 23.6k |\n| 3 | `anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5` | ★★★ | 10 | 10 | 7 | 10 | 9.4s | 8.5k |\n| 4 | `gemini:gemini-2.5-flash` | ★★★ | 10 | 7 | 5 | 9 | 7.3s | 6.9k |\n| 5 | `ollama:nemotron-cascade-2` | ★★★ | 10 | 9 | 5 | 5 | 60.4s | 11.7k |\n| 6 | `openai:gpt-4o-mini` | ★★☆ | 10 | 8 | 8 | 10 | 19.2s | 8.7k |\n| 7 | `ollama:gemma4:31b` | ★★☆ | 10 | 8 | 4 | 5 | 264.2s | 6.4k |\n\n**Columns**\n\n- **Stars** — overall weighted rating (1-3) combining accuracy, comprehensiveness, code quality, code-mode efficiency, speed, token efficiency, and stability.\n- **Acc / Comp / TS / CME** — Anthropic-judged subscores out of 10: accuracy vs gold, comprehensiveness, TypeScript quality, code-mode efficiency (fewer wasted attempts is better).\n- **Latency** — wall-clock time for the full agentic loop.\n- **Tokens** — total prompt + completion tokens. Grok's adapter does not report usage.\n\n**Takeaways**\n\n- **Strongest cloud picks:** Grok 4.1 Fast, Claude Haiku 4.5, and Gemini 2.5 Flash all finish under 10s and handle the multi-step task cleanly. Claude Haiku 4.5 has the highest comprehensiveness score (10/10).\n- **Strongest local pick:** `ollama:gpt-oss:20b` is the best local performer at 45s with zero compilation failures. `ollama:nemotron-cascade-2` is a close second.\n- **Avoid:** the smaller `gemma4` (9.6 GB) and the other local models commented out at the top of `eval-config.ts` (`granite4:3b`, `ministral-3`, `mistral:7b`, `qwen3:8b`, etc.) — they either ignore the `external_queryTable` shape, hallucinate results, or refuse to invoke `execute_typescript`.\n- **Caveat:** this is a single‑prompt benchmark. Local model results can vary noticeably between runs; use these as a rough capability filter rather than a definitive ranking.\n\nReproduce locally:\n\n```bash\ncd packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval\npnpm install\npnpm eval                    # full suite (needs cloud API keys + Anthropic for judging)\npnpm eval -- --ollama-only   # local models only\npnpm eval -- --no-judge      # skip Anthropic-based judging\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Start simple.** Give the model 2-3 tools and a clear task. Code Mode works best when the model has a focused set of capabilities.\n- **Prefer `Promise.all` tasks.** Code Mode shines when the model can parallelize work that would otherwise be sequential tool calls.\n- **Use `console.log` for debugging.** Logs are captured and returned in the result, making it easy to see what happened inside the sandbox.\n- **Keep tools focused.** Each tool should do one thing well. The model will compose them in code.\n- **Check the system prompt.** Call `createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)` and inspect the output to see exactly what the model will see, including generated type stubs.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration) — Display execution progress in your React app\n- [Code Mode with Snippets](./code-mode-with-snippets) — Add persistent, reusable snippet libraries\n- [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates): compare Node, QuickJS, QuickJS Bun, Cloudflare, Daytona, and E2B.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Code Mode\nid: code-mode\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Let LLMs write and execute TypeScript programs that orchestrate tools in a secure sandbox with TanStack AI Code Mode — fewer loops, richer logic.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - code mode\n  - sandbox\n  - typescript execution\n  - tool orchestration\n  - execute_typescript\n  - ai agents\n---\n\nCode Mode lets an LLM write and execute TypeScript programs inside a secure sandbox. Instead of making one tool call at a time, the model writes a short script that orchestrates multiple tools with loops, conditionals, `Promise.all`, and data transformations — then returns a single result.\n\nYou already have a chat app that uses [tools](../tools/tools). By the end of this guide, you'll have Code Mode set up so the LLM can compose those tools in TypeScript and execute them in a single sandbox call.\n\n## Why Code Mode?\n\n### Reduced context window usage\n\nIn a traditional agentic loop, every tool call adds a round-trip of messages: the model's tool-call request, the tool result, then the model's next reasoning step. A task that touches five tools can easily consume thousands of tokens in back-and-forth.\n\nWith Code Mode the model emits one `execute_typescript` call containing a complete program. The five tool invocations happen inside the sandbox, and only the final result comes back — one request, one response.\n\n### The LLM decides how to interpret tool output\n\nWhen tools are called individually, the model must decide what to do with each result in a new turn. With Code Mode, the model writes the logic up front: filter, aggregate, compare, branch. It can `Promise.all` ten API calls, pick the best result, and return a summary — all in a single execution.\n\n### Type-safe tool execution\n\nTools you pass to Code Mode are converted to typed function stubs that appear in the system prompt. The model sees exact input/output types, so it generates correct calls without guessing parameter names or shapes. TypeScript annotations in the generated code are stripped automatically before execution.\n\n### Secure sandboxing\n\nGenerated code runs in an isolated environment. V8, QuickJS WASM, native QuickJS on Bun, and a Cloudflare Worker have no access to the host file system, network, or process. A Daytona sandbox and an E2B sandbox are full Linux environments. Each sandbox has its own file system, network, and processes. The code in that sandbox cannot reach the host. Timeouts and memory limits are configurable.\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### 1. Install packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-code-mode zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPick an isolate driver:\n\nNode.js (V8 isolates, native compile):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-node\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nQuickJS WASM (browsers and edge, no native deps):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nQuickJS Bun (native QuickJS via bun:ffi):\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nCloudflare Workers:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nDaytona sandboxes:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona @daytona/sdk\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nE2B sandboxes:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nvue: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\npreact: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nangular: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\noctane: @tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b e2b\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Define tools\n\nDefine your tools with `toolDefinition()` and provide a server-side implementation with `.server()`. These become the `external_*` functions available inside the sandbox.\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst fetchWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"fetchWeather\",\n  description: \"Get current weather for a city\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ location: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    condition: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`https://api.weather.example/v1?city=${location}`);\n  return res.json();\n});\n```\n\n### 3. Create the Code Mode tool and system prompt\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { createCodeMode } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { createNodeIsolateDriver } from \"@tanstack/ai-isolate-node\";\n\nconst { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver: createNodeIsolateDriver(),\n  tools: [fetchWeather],\n  timeout: 30_000,\n});\n```\n\n### 4. Use with `chat()`\n\n```typescript group=code-mode\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nconst result = await chat({\n  adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n  systemPrompts: [\n    \"You are a helpful weather assistant.\",\n    systemPrompt,\n  ],\n  tools: [tool],\n  messages: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      content: \"Compare the weather in Tokyo, Paris, and New York City\",\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nThe model will generate something like:\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst cities = [\"Tokyo\", \"Paris\", \"New York City\"];\nconst results = await Promise.all(\n  cities.map((city) => external_fetchWeather({ location: city }))\n);\n\nconst warmest = results.reduce((prev, curr) =>\n  curr.temperature > prev.temperature ? curr : prev\n);\n\nreturn {\n  comparison: results.map((r, i) => ({\n    city: cities[i],\n    temperature: r.temperature,\n    condition: r.condition,\n  })),\n  warmest: cities[results.indexOf(warmest)],\n};\n```\n\nAll three API calls happen in parallel inside the sandbox. The model receives one structured result instead of three separate tool-call round-trips.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `createCodeMode(config)`\n\nCreates both the `execute_typescript` tool and its matching system prompt from a single config object. This is the recommended entry point.\n\n```typescript ignore\nconst { tool, systemPrompt } = createCodeMode({\n  driver,          // IsolateDriver — required\n  tools,           // Array<ServerTool | ToolDefinition> — required, at least one\n  timeout,         // number — execution timeout in ms (default: 30000)\n  memoryLimit,     // number. Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers.\n  getSnippetBindings, // () => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>> — optional dynamic bindings\n});\n```\n\n**Config properties:**\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `driver` | `IsolateDriver` | The sandbox runtime to execute code in |\n| `tools` | `Array<ServerTool \\| ToolDefinition>` | Tools exposed as `external_*` functions. Must have `.server()` implementations |\n| `timeout` | `number` | Execution timeout in milliseconds (default: 30000) |\n| `memoryLimit` | `number` | Memory limit in MB (default: 128). Supported by Node, QuickJS, and E2B drivers |\n| `getSnippetBindings` | `() => Promise<Record<string, ToolBinding>>` | Optional function returning additional bindings at execution time |\n| `debug` | `DebugOption` | Debug logging, same shape as `chat({ debug })`. Failed executions log under `errors` (on by default), successful ones under `tools`. Pass `{ logger }` to use your own `Logger`, or `false` to silence. See [Debug Logging](../advanced/debug-logging.md) |\n\nThe tool returns a `CodeModeToolResult`:\n\n```typescript\ninterface CodeModeToolResult {\n  success: boolean;\n  result?: unknown;    // Return value from the executed code\n  logs?: Array<string>; // Captured console output\n  error?: {\n    message: string;\n    name?: string;\n    line?: number;\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### `createCodeModeTool(config)` / `createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)`\n\nLower-level functions if you need only the tool or only the prompt. `createCodeMode` calls both internally.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCodeModeTool, createCodeModeSystemPrompt } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\nimport { config } from \"./config\";\n\nconst tool = createCodeModeTool(config);\nconst prompt = createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config);\n```\n\n### `IsolateDriver`\n\nThe interface that sandbox runtimes implement. You do not implement this yourself — pick one of the provided drivers:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { IsolateConfig, IsolateContext } from \"@tanstack/ai-code-mode\";\n\ninterface IsolateDriver {\n  createContext(config: IsolateConfig): Promise<IsolateContext>;\n}\n```\n\n**Available drivers:**\n\n| Package | Factory function | Environment |\n|---------|-----------------|-------------|\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-node` | `createNodeIsolateDriver()` | Node.js |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs` | `createQuickJSIsolateDriver()` | Node.js, browser, edge |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-quickjs-bun` | `createQuickJSBunIsolateDriver()` | Bun |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-cloudflare` | `createCloudflareIsolateDriver()` | Cloudflare Workers |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-daytona` | `createDaytonaIsolateDriver()` | Daytona sandboxes |\n| `@tanstack/ai-isolate-e2b` | `createE2BIsolateDriver()` | E2B sandboxes |\n\nFor full configuration options for each driver, see [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates.md).\n\n### Advanced\n\nThese utilities are used internally and are exported for custom pipelines:\n\n- **`stripTypeScript(code)`** — Strips TypeScript syntax using sucrase (edge-safe, no native binary), converting to plain JavaScript.\n- **`toolsToBindings(tools, prefix?)`** — Converts TanStack AI tools into `Record<string, ToolBinding>` for sandbox injection.\n- **`generateTypeStubs(bindings, options?)`** — Generates TypeScript type declarations from tool bindings for system prompts.\n\n## Choosing a Driver\n\nFor a full comparison of drivers with all configuration options, see [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates.md).\n\nIn brief: use the **Node driver** for server-side Node.js (fastest, V8 JIT), **QuickJS** for browsers or portable edge deployments (no native deps), **QuickJS Bun** for Bun servers (native QuickJS via `bun:ffi`), the **Cloudflare driver** when you deploy to Cloudflare Workers, and the **Daytona driver** when you want execution inside a full remote Linux sandbox.\n\nUse the **E2B driver** for an E2B sandbox.\n\n## Custom Events\n\nCode Mode emits custom events during execution that you can observe through the TanStack AI event system. These are useful for building UIs that show execution progress, debugging, or logging.\n\n| Event | When | Payload |\n|-------|------|---------|\n| `code_mode:execution_started` | Code execution begins | `{ timestamp, codeLength }` |\n| `code_mode:console` | Each `console.log/error/warn/info` call | `{ level, message, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:external_call` | Before an `external_*` function runs | `{ function, args, timestamp }` |\n| `code_mode:external_result` | After a successful `external_*` call | `{ function, result, duration }` |\n| `code_mode:external_error` | When an `external_*` call fails | `{ function, error, duration }` |\n\nTo display these events in your React app, see [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration).\n\n## Stop tool calls when the run stops\n\nWhen a user stops a chat run, a tool call that the sandbox started keeps going unless the tool listens for the abort. Each `external_*` call gets the `abortSignal` of the chat run in its second argument. Pass it to the slow work:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst searchDocs = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"searchDocs\",\n  description: \"Search the docs\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ query }, ctx) => {\n  const res = await fetch(\n    `https://search.example/v1?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,\n    { signal: ctx?.abortSignal },\n  );\n  return res.json();\n});\n```\n\nMCP tools from `@tanstack/ai-mcp` already stop their request when the run aborts.\n\nA tool that runs inside Code Mode gets these fields:\n\n- `abortSignal`: the signal of the chat run. If the run is already aborted, the call does not start.\n- `context`: the runtime `context` that you gave to `chat()`.\n- `emitCustomEvent`: sends a custom event to the stream. A tool that a `snippet_*` function calls does not send events.\n\nThe tool does not get `toolCallId` or `inputResponse`. These fields belong to the `execute_typescript` call.\n\n## Model Compatibility\n\nCode Mode asks the model to write valid TypeScript that calls your tools through the sandbox bridge. Not every model handles this equally — many small or older models mishandle the `external_*` calling conventions even when the system prompt is explicit. We track a single multi-step benchmark (joining three tables, filtering customers who bought from every product category, aggregating spend per category) against a gold reference. The full harness lives at `packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval/`.\n\n| Rank | Model | Stars | Acc | Comp | TS | CME | Latency | Tokens |\n|------|-------|:-----:|:---:|:----:|:--:|:---:|--------:|-------:|\n| 1 | `grok:grok-4-1-fast-non-reasoning` | ★★★ | 10 | 9 | 6 | 10 | 7.0s | — |\n| 2 | `ollama:gpt-oss:20b` | ★★★ | 10 | 8 | 6 | 5 | 45.1s | 23.6k |\n| 3 | `anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5` | ★★★ | 10 | 10 | 7 | 10 | 9.4s | 8.5k |\n| 4 | `gemini:gemini-2.5-flash` | ★★★ | 10 | 7 | 5 | 9 | 7.3s | 6.9k |\n| 5 | `ollama:nemotron-cascade-2` | ★★★ | 10 | 9 | 5 | 5 | 60.4s | 11.7k |\n| 6 | `openai:gpt-4o-mini` | ★★☆ | 10 | 8 | 8 | 10 | 19.2s | 8.7k |\n| 7 | `ollama:gemma4:31b` | ★★☆ | 10 | 8 | 4 | 5 | 264.2s | 6.4k |\n\n**Columns**\n\n- **Stars** — overall weighted rating (1-3) combining accuracy, comprehensiveness, code quality, code-mode efficiency, speed, token efficiency, and stability.\n- **Acc / Comp / TS / CME** — Anthropic-judged subscores out of 10: accuracy vs gold, comprehensiveness, TypeScript quality, code-mode efficiency (fewer wasted attempts is better).\n- **Latency** — wall-clock time for the full agentic loop.\n- **Tokens** — total prompt + completion tokens. Grok's adapter does not report usage.\n\n**Takeaways**\n\n- **Strongest cloud picks:** Grok 4.1 Fast, Claude Haiku 4.5, and Gemini 2.5 Flash all finish under 10s and handle the multi-step task cleanly. Claude Haiku 4.5 has the highest comprehensiveness score (10/10).\n- **Strongest local pick:** `ollama:gpt-oss:20b` is the best local performer at 45s with zero compilation failures. `ollama:nemotron-cascade-2` is a close second.\n- **Avoid:** the smaller `gemma4` (9.6 GB) and the other local models commented out at the top of `eval-config.ts` (`granite4:3b`, `ministral-3`, `mistral:7b`, `qwen3:8b`, etc.) — they either ignore the `external_queryTable` shape, hallucinate results, or refuse to invoke `execute_typescript`.\n- **Caveat:** this is a single‑prompt benchmark. Local model results can vary noticeably between runs; use these as a rough capability filter rather than a definitive ranking.\n\nReproduce locally:\n\n```bash\ncd packages/ai-code-mode/models-eval\npnpm install\npnpm eval                    # full suite (needs cloud API keys + Anthropic for judging)\npnpm eval -- --ollama-only   # local models only\npnpm eval -- --no-judge      # skip Anthropic-based judging\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Start simple.** Give the model 2-3 tools and a clear task. Code Mode works best when the model has a focused set of capabilities.\n- **Prefer `Promise.all` tasks.** Code Mode shines when the model can parallelize work that would otherwise be sequential tool calls.\n- **Use `console.log` for debugging.** Logs are captured and returned in the result, making it easy to see what happened inside the sandbox.\n- **Keep tools focused.** Each tool should do one thing well. The model will compose them in code.\n- **Check the system prompt.** Call `createCodeModeSystemPrompt(config)` and inspect the output to see exactly what the model will see, including generated type stubs.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Showing Code Mode in the UI](./client-integration) — Display execution progress in your React app\n- [Code Mode with Snippets](./code-mode-with-snippets) — Add persistent, reusable snippet libraries\n- [Isolate Drivers](./code-mode-isolates): compare Node, QuickJS, QuickJS Bun, Cloudflare, Daytona, and E2B.\n"}
